      "reasoning": "Articles 65 and 67 of Additional Protocol I specifically regulate 'civil defence' or 'civilian civil defence' personnel. The facts identify the actors as 'reserve police' and members of a 'private security agency.' These are not civil defence units as defined in AP I. Citing these articles to define the status of police forces is a misapplication of the treaty text; police forces in an IAC are generally treated as combatants or associated forces, not protected civilian civil defence personnel.",
